    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan presents a genuinely balanced case for AAPL, with credible arguments on both sides. The bear makes a stronger technical case (price below all major moving averages, death cross in place, RSI at 37, no identifiable catalyst), but the bull's counterpoints carry real weight \u2014 MACD histogram contraction from -1.41 to -0.06 signals a 96% reduction in selling pressure, support at $167.18 has held across three tests, and the fundamentals are strong ($39.9B quarterly operating cash flow, $11.2B net cash build). The bear's SELL/SHORT call is too aggressive given strong cash generation and proven support, while the bull's BUY is premature given the confirmed downtrend and absence of a catalyst. The risk/reward is roughly symmetric at current levels (~$170.76), making Hold the most defensible stance. For existing holders, a defined risk stop below proven support at $167.18 (near $166.50, ~2.5% risk) protects against a support break, while confirmation triggers (reclaim of 50 SMA at $181.19 or break below $167.18) would justify directional action.\n\n**Entry Price**: 170.76\n\n**Stop Loss**: 166.5\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral weight \u2014 no more than a modest position given the balanced setup\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
